Z||000001||Carrolles||05-17-2000||11:35 PM||||About three weeks after I installed my new 2.8 it started doing the same thing.  I replaced the IAC and temp sensor like the codes called for but it didn't help.  I finally got frustrated and took it to the Pontiac dealership.  They took three hours of diagnostics and found that the ECM was going out.  A new ECM and everything is ok now.  Total bill was around $325 most of which was diagnostics time.||||reg||1
